WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:03.620
77 year old billionaire Robert Kraft is accused

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:05.840
We’ve all heard that New England Patriots owner

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:09.180
Robert Kraft was caught in a sex trafficking sting.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:12.180
Women at the spas were lured into the sex trade.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:14.480
They were women who were from China,

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.220
who were forced into sex slavery.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:18.440
We’re told it happens all the time.

00:00:18.449 --> 00:00:20.980
Thousands of children are raped every day.

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:23.700
Sex trafficking, a growing problem.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.640
But that’s not true, says reporter Elizabeth Nolan Brown.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.680
In Robert Kraft’s case:

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:31.100
They had all of these big announcements at first saying

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.040
that they had bust up

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.520
an international sex trafficking ring,

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:36.520
that these women were being forced there

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:37.460
and they weren’t allowed to leave.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:40.700
This is not about lonely old man or victimless crimes.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:45.980
This is about enabling a network of criminals to

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:50.780
traffic women into our country for forced labor and sex.

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:53.040
But now prosecutors concede

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.980
there was no sex trafficking.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:57.400
And that’s typical.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:00.060
I'd say 99% of the headlines are not true.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.420
Sex trafficking and prostitution

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:03.260
are just sort of used interchangeably.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:07.280
We're here to rescue people that need to be rescued.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:10.409
Police routinely claim they rescue women.

00:01:10.409 --> 00:01:12.240
They say “we rescued these women” and by rescue

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.460
they put them in jail and give them a criminal record.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.640
The victims are the sex workers themselves who are

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:20.180
getting harassed and locked up in cages by the cops.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.720
Agents arresting at least 14 suspects.

00:01:23.729 --> 00:01:25.360
Being arrested doesn’t help you.

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:28.130
These women chose to be sex workers.

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:29.980
I wasn't coerced.

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.490
It was something that I actively wanted to do.

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:34.880
But the cops call it sex trafficking.

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:36.130
You were trafficked.

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:39.240
Yeah, they call a lot of things trafficking,

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:42.090
the drug trafficking, the immigration trafficking.

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:44.000
Celebrities perpetuate the myth.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.680
Today you can go online and buy a child for sex.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:49.400
It's as easy as ordering a pizza.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.080
Human trafficking is

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:55.800
the fastest growing illegal business in the world.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.760
If that was the case, cops would be able

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:58.880
to find this all the time,

00:01:58.880 --> 00:01:59.800
cops wouldn't be having to

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:00.900
go through these elaborate

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:01.960
doing these elaborate stings.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:03.700
Florida police spent months

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:05.940
taking down the Robert Kraft spa.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:07.749
They had Homeland Security involved,

00:02:07.749 --> 00:02:08.920
they were following these women around

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.960
the grocery stores, watching them buy condoms,

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:12.620
they were going through their trash

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:14.100
and analyzing their trash.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.100
If this was really a situation where these women

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.540
were being forced and sexually assaulted

00:02:18.549 --> 00:02:19.540
multiple times a day,

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:22.810
the cops just let it happen for months on end?

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:24.520
The women were trafficked.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:29.160
In case after case, police call the women “sex slaves.”

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.880
These women are true victims.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:33.820
I actually talked to one of the sheriffs

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:34.600
who was interviewed there

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:37.300
the first one, John Urquhart, and he ended up saying,

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:40.330
“Well, you know, I mean maybe they weren't being forced

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:42.660
by whatever, but we're all trafficked by something

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:43.960
and there was money involved,

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:46.280
and then by the end of the investigation they were like,

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:48.800
“Well, I mean, they were pressured because they didn't

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:51.000
know a lot of people and they wanted to make money,”

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.120
The implication is,

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:54.800
with the number of men and the number of hours,

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:56.780
that this couldn't have been voluntary.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:58.620
I read through all the court documents involved in this,

00:02:58.629 --> 00:03:01.950
and it actually paints a very, very different story.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:03.360
The documents, as usual,

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:05.420
made reference to prostitution.

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:07.629
The women apparently were willing.

00:03:07.629 --> 00:03:10.219
We wanted to rescue them out of that horrible life.

00:03:10.219 --> 00:03:12.320
They are on a moral crusade.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:14.200
They're doing the right thing.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.520
But all they did was actually go in there,

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:17.780
bust up their place of business,

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:19.380
close it down, and then let the women go.

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:22.900
The cops are not cruel, they, I assume

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:24.340
they want to do the right thing.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:27.280
Why would they say this stuff?

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:29.340
Cops like working these kinds of cases, I think.

00:03:29.349 --> 00:03:31.560
They bring the police good publicity

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.239
A major sex trafficking ring busted

00:03:34.239 --> 00:03:34.940
And also…

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:37.220
You have a lot of federal money coming at this.

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:38.940
These human trafficking task forces

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:40.040
where the federal government funds

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:42.480
these local cops to do these stings,

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:44.480
and if they call them human trafficking stings,

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:45.300
they get this money.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:49.020
So much of the anti-prostitution laws that

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:51.180
are being pushed is a combination

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.560
of the conservative fetish

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:56.120
for going after people for doing “sex stuff"

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:59.640
and the liberal instinct to help a group of people

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:01.500
that they can't be bothered to understand.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:04.269
Trafficking is a real problem in every state

00:04:04.269 --> 00:04:05.760
in the United States of America.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:09.980
Right now almost 300,000 American children are at risk.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:11.520
300,000 children.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.700
300,000

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:16.580
Not just at risk, says this former prosecutor:

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:21.760
300,000 kids a year are raped, sex trafficked,

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:23.460
and pimped in this country.

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:25.260
That 300,000 number

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:26.740
was disavowed.

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:28.600
The lead author of the study, Richard Estes,

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:29.880
now disavows it,

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:32.540
the National Crimes Against Children Center says

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:33.860
do not cite this study.

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:35.720
So many people debunk the study and say

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:38.120
this is just a total bull crap number.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:41.020
I'd like to tell you a story about a 15-year old girl

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:43.740
Actor Ashton Kutcher even promotes an app

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:46.700
which he claims rescues sex trafficking victims.

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:48.680
We’ve identified and recovered

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:52.360
over 6,000 trafficking victims this year.

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:54.260
Ashton Kutcher has this app….

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.040
[ugh]

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:57.240
which he claims recovers victims.

00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:59.920
300,000 children are at risk.

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:01.980
Where is he getting these numbers?

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:03.900
If Ashton Kutcher is finding all those victims,

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:05.040
he's not turning them over to police.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:07.280
Kutcher’s representatives did not respond

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.180
to our repeated emails.

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:11.500
When we have these exaggerated numbers,

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:13.160
it forces people to go into this

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:15.740
crazy emergency moral panic mode that

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:18.420
ends up not helping the actual problem that we have.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:19.700
If it was your daughter there

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:22.160
you would not be saying it’s a victimless crime.

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:23.860
They want to just eradicate all prostitution.

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:26.160
We will not stop until we have stamped out

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:28.320
the menace of human trafficking.

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:31.160
They want this imaginary world where if you take away

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:33.260
you know, a safer option for these women

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:34.360
and everyone will just,

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:36.620
the oldest profession as they call it, will magically stop.

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:38.380
But that's not going to happen.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:40.980
They are treating the women like a piece of furniture.

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:43.440
The way we try to stop that from happening,

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:45.460
is actually making the problem worse.

